- feature_id: v3.responses_direct_mvp_architecture
  status: p6_source_and_local_live_verified
  change_risk: high
  owner_kind: rust_project_v3
  owner_scope: P6 generic Responses direct Runtime/Provider lifecycle after verified P0-P5 foundation
  owner_modules:
  - v3/crates/routecodex-v3-runtime
  - v3/crates/routecodex-v3-provider-responses
  - v3/crates/routecodex-v3-server
  design:
  - docs/design/v3-system-definition.md
  - docs/goals/v3-foundation-implementation-order.md
  - docs/goals/v3-responses-direct-mvp-implementation-plan.md
  - docs/goals/v3-vr-target-protocol-execution-decision-sop.md
  test_design:
  - docs/goals/v3-responses-direct-mvp-test-design.md
  - docs/goals/v3-direct-thinking-tag-response-compat-test-design.md
  required_contract:
  - P6 owns only adjacent transitions V3Target10ConcreteProviderSelected through V3Server16HttpFrame, with V3Execution11ProtocolDecision between Target10 and Direct policy
  - Runtime remains the only complete lifecycle executor
  - routecodex-v3-provider-responses is generic and contains no deployment provider ID or provider-family branch
  - Server and CLI cannot import or call Provider transport
  - no relay continuation servertool other protocol V2 compatibility fallback repair sanitize or raw replay
  - v3-rd-10 through v3-rd-12 may be anchored only by the generic Provider runtime source and controlled-upstream evidence
  - V3Execution11ProtocolDecision is written by protocol execution planning before initial dispatch and recomputed only for the currently selected Target10 after provider failure reselection; continuation
    owner remains the only Direct/Relay lock
  - V3Target10ConcreteProviderSelected carries provider.responses.process; selected Responses providers with process=chat must choose Hub Relay before SameProtocolDirect during protocol execution planning
  - P6 Dry Run invokes the same Runtime kernel and replaces only the Provider transport with a no-network effect
  - Direct provider errors enter the shared Error01-06/provider-health policy; success payload semantics remain provider-owned while client transport projection follows the client stream intent
  - Direct provider raw response decode/projection errors enter the same Error01-06 provider failure policy and reselect before Error06 while alternatives remain
  - Direct target-local reselection uses the full captured Target09 candidate set; if the newly selected Target10 requires Hub Relay and no Direct-owned previous_response_id is active, Direct returns a
    typed relay handoff side-channel carrying the complete request-local failed-candidate exclusion set so Relay cannot retry an already-failed Direct target
  - Direct server execution passes the server-scoped provider health store so cross-request cooldown affects subsequent selection
  - Direct server observability derives JSON finish_reason from parsed response status only for log/usage output; non-stream JSON client bodies are not mutated, while stream requests may project valid provider
    JSON as client SSE without treating provider inbound transport as client protocol truth
  - Client stream requests keep text/event-stream for Error06 and success frames; non-stream requests keep JSON while valid provider JSON may omit top-level finish_reason
  required_gates:
  - npm run render:v3-mainline-caller-flow
  - npm run verify:v3-mainline-caller-flow
  - npm run test:v3-mainline-caller-flow-red-fixtures
  - npm run verify:architecture-wiki-html-sync
  - npm run verify:v3-architecture-docs
  - npm run verify:v3-rust-only
  - npm run verify:v3-module-boundaries
  - npm run test:v3-source-gate-red-fixtures
  - npm run verify:v3-static-hook-registry
  - npm run verify:v3-resource-map
  - npm run test:v3-compile-fail
  - npm run test:v3-provider-responses
  - npm run test:v3-direct-protocol-plan-session-cooldown
  - npm run test:v3-responses-process-execution-decision
  - npm run test:v3-responses-direct-unit
  - npm run test:v3-responses-direct-blackbox
  - npm run test:v3-direct-sse-compile
  - npm run test:v3-direct-response-observability
  - npm run verify:v3-cargo-fmt
  - npm run verify:v3-clippy
  - npm run test:v3-workspace
