- feature_id: v3.responses_provider_runtime
  status: source_verified_controlled_upstream
  change_risk: high
  owner_kind: rust_project_v3
  owner_scope: 'Generic Rust Provider runtime slice for Responses entry: selected Target with provider_type -> provider wire -> protocol-specific transport request -> typed raw response/source error'
  owner_modules:
  - v3/crates/routecodex-v3-provider-responses
  - v3/crates/routecodex-v3-runtime
  - v3/crates/routecodex-v3-target
  design:
  - docs/goals/v3-responses-direct-mvp-implementation-plan.md
  - docs/goals/v3-responses-direct-mvp-test-design.md
  contract:
  - docs/architecture/v3-resource-operation-map.yml
  - docs/architecture/v3-mainline-call-map.yml
  - docs/architecture/wiki/v3-responses-direct-mainline.md
  test_design:
  - docs/goals/v3-responses-direct-mvp-test-design.md
  required_unit:
  - Provider wire preserves the complete client history byte-for-byte, including historical tool-output images and reasoning encrypted content; only the selected wire model binding and current-turn validation
    may differ
  - 'The Responses continuation save->restore interval is immutable: Resp04 commit through next Req04 restore only projects, frames, transports, validates scope, or releases; SSE transport, server handler,
    client body adapter, and store transport must not clean, convert, reorder, patch, or restore history'
  - Provider wire rejects malformed current-turn data:image payloads before Provider transport and projects them as client input errors, while valid current images remain normal payload
  - Provider transport resolves env and token-file auth only at send boundary
  - Provider raw response preserves JSON bytes and validated SSE event bytes
  - Provider HTTP transport accepts application/json raw response bodies for SSE-intent requests while preserving request-side Accept/stream SSE intent
  - Provider HTTP transport rejects text/event-stream raw responses for JSON-intent requests instead of silently switching provider response kind
  - Provider transport dispatches by selected provider_type; Anthropic targets use /v1/messages, x-api-key, anthropic-version, Anthropic wire, and Responses client projection
  - Provider errors stay typed for missing auth, HTTP status, transport failure, malformed SSE, and client disconnect
  - 'Adaptive provider concurrency is keyed by providerId plus authAlias: below budget leases send immediately, the first over-budget request is a real probe, HTTP 429 confirms saturation, and no acquire
    timeout fabricates a local failure'
  - A successful ten-minute probe increases the budget, a 429 probe decreases it, and SSE leases release only when the raw stream is dropped or exhausted
  required_contract:
  - routecodex-v3-provider-responses remains generic across provider IDs and may branch only by provider_type/protocol, never by deployment provider ID
  - Provider consumes an already selected target and never reads config, Virtual Router, Target interpreter, route groups, or Forwarder resources
  - Server and CLI cannot import Provider transport
  - Provider node structs 12, 13, and 14 cannot be constructed by non-owner code
  - auth secret values never enter manifest, Debug, Error, Provider wire Debug, transport request Debug, or client payload
  required_gates:
  - npm run test:v3-provider-responses
  - npm run test:v3-provider-adaptive-concurrency
  - npm run test:v3-responses-direct-blackbox
  - npm run test:v3-provider-health-contract
  - npm run verify:v3-module-boundaries
  - npm run test:v3-source-gate-red-fixtures
  - npm run test:v3-compile-fail
  - npm run verify:v3-architecture-docs
  - npm run verify:v3-rust-only
  - npm run verify:v3-static-hook-registry
  - npm run verify:v3-resource-map
  - npm run verify:v3-cargo-fmt
  - npm run verify:v3-clippy
  - npm run test:v3-workspace
